## Solution

**Setup.** Place $B=(0,0)$, $C=(13,0)$. From $AB=14$, $AC=15$:
$$x_A^2+y_A^2=196,\quad (x_A-13)^2+y_A^2=225 \implies x_A=\tfrac{70}{13},\; y_A=\tfrac{168}{13}.$$
So $A=\left(\frac{70}{13},\frac{168}{13}\right)$. The area is $\sqrt{21\cdot 8\cdot 7\cdot 6}=84$, semiperimeter $s=21$, inradius $r=4$.

**Incenter and contact points.** The incenter (side-length weighted) is
$$I=\frac{13A+15B+14C}{42}=\frac{(70,168)+(182,0)}{42}=(6,4),$$
consistent with $r=4$ (distance to $BC$). The contact point on $BC$ is $D=(6,0)$ (since $BD=s-b=6$).

The contact point on $AB$ ($BF=6$): $F=\frac{6}{14}A=\left(\frac{30}{13},\frac{72}{13}\right)$.

The contact point on $AC$ ($CE=7$): $E=C+\frac{7}{15}(A-C)=\left(\frac{614}{65},\frac{392}{65}\right)$.

Then
$$E-F=\left(\frac{464}{65},\frac{32}{65}\right)\propto (29,2),$$
so line $EF$ has direction $(29,2)$.

**Point $X$: midpoint of major arc $\widehat{BAC}$.** The circumcenter lies on $x=\frac{13}{2}$; solving gives $O=\left(\frac{13}{2},\frac{507}{104}\right)$ with $R=\frac{65}{8}$. The perpendicular bisector of $BC$ meets the circle at $\left(\frac{13}{2},\frac{507}{104}\pm\frac{65}{8}\right)$, i.e. $\left(\frac{13}{2},13\right)$ and $\left(\frac{13}{2},-\frac{169}{52}\right)$. Since $\angle A=\arccos\frac{3}{5}\approx 53.1^\circ$, arc $BC$ not containing $A$ is the minor arc ($\approx 106^\circ$), so the arc through $A$ is major. Its midpoint (on the same side as $A$) is
$$X=\left(\frac{13}{2},13\right).$$

**Line $XI$.** Direction $X-I=\left(\frac12,9\right)\propto(1,18)$. Points on $XI$: $(6+u,\;4+18u)$.

**Condition $DP\perp EF$.** With $P=(6+u,4+18u)$ and $D=(6,0)$:
$$P-D=(u,\;4+18u),\qquad (P-D)\cdot(29,2)=29u+2(4+18u)=65u+8=0,$$
so $u=-\frac{8}{65}$, giving $P=\left(\frac{382}{65},\frac{116}{65}\right)$.

**Compute $DP$.**
$$P-D=\left(-\frac{8}{65},\frac{116}{65}\right),\quad DP=\frac{\sqrt{64+116^2}}{65}=\frac{\sqrt{13520}}{65}=\frac{52\sqrt{5}}{65}=\frac{4\sqrt{5}}{5}.$$

$$\boxed{DP=\dfrac{4\sqrt{5}}{5}}$$

### PROOF COMPLETE
